<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ordu-Baliq</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Karabalgasun</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ordu-Baliq was the capital of the Uyghur Khaganate on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orkhon-river">Orkhon River</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a>, built in the mid-8th century under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayanchur-khan">Bayanchur Khan</a>. Its ruins, known as Karabalgasun, include massive walls, a citadel and a palace, and travellers described a walled city surrounded by farmland and markets. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yenisei-kyrgyz">Yenisei Kyrgyz</a> sacked it in 840, ending the khaganate.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ordu-baliq.jpg" alt="Ordu-Baliq" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: James A. Glazier · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ordu-baliq.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
